    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mankato/Director-of-Curriculum-Management---Management-Analyst-3--AA26153-_JR0000005446": {
      "title": "Director of Curriculum Management - Management Analyst 3 (AA26153)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Director of Curriculum Management - Management Analyst 3 (AA26153) Institution: Minnesota State University, Mankato Classification Title: Management Analyst 3 Bargaining Unit / Union: 214: Minnesota Association of Professional Employees City: Mankato FLSA: Non Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Classified - Unlimited Salary Range: $28.75 - $42.16 Salary Range: $28.75 - $42.16 / hourly; $60,030 - $88,030 / annually Job Description The Director of Curriculum Management provides leadership, coordination, and oversight of the university’s curriculum development and approval processes. This position ensures the accuracy, integrity, and consistency of academic program information across all institutional systems, supports faculty and academic units in developing and revising curricula with an equity lens, and serves as the central point of contact for curriculum policy, governance workflows, and compliance requirements. The Director collaborates closely with Academic Affairs, Registrar’s Office, Institutional Research, accreditation teams, and academic colleges to ensure that curriculum processes are efficient, transparent, and aligned with institutional goals and regulatory standards. The position supports departments with market research and viability analysis to inform decisions about new and existing academic programs. Through strong communication, project management, and collaboration, the Director ensures that curriculum processes are efficient, compliant, and supportive of institutional goals. Minimum Qualifications Substantial experience (three or more years) in curriculum development, academic planning, or academic program management in a higher education setting.  Demonstrated ability to apply an equity lens to program and curriculum design, academic portfolio management, and analysis of demand for academic programs. Strong project management skills, including the ability to manage complex initiatives, coordinate across departments, and meet institutional deadlines.  Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, including the ability to collaborate with diverse stakeholders including faculty, staff, and administrators; to present complex information clearly and concisely; and to develop recommendations and technical reports for non-technical users and for specialist users as appropriate. Experience with curriculum management systems, academic planning tools, student information systems, and large databases and the ability to guide their effective use across the institution.  Demonstrated ability to analyze and communicate curriculum-related data to inform executive decision-making and long-term academic planning, including market analysis and recommendations for curriculum development. Demonstrated ability to interpret and apply academic policies, accreditation standards, and regulatory requirements related to curriculum and program development. Preferred Qualification  Master’s or doctoral degree in any discipline (Conferred on an official transcript at the time of application). Demonstrated commitment to fostering a diverse working and learning environment. Demonstrated success in facilitating professional development or institutional training related to curriculum design, academic planning, or program review. Familiarity with the Minnesota State Colleges and Universities system, including ISRS or Workday, and system-level curriculum policies and procedures. Knowledge of state, federal, and accrediting body requirements for academic programs at all levels (undergraduate, graduate, and professional). Experience managing or supporting transitions in academic systems, such as student information systems or catalog platforms. Other Requirements Please note that successful applicants must be eligible to work in the United States on or before the effective date of appointment. Eligibility includes being a U.S. citizen or national, a lawful permanent resident, or a foreign national authorized to work in the U.S. without the need for employer sponsorship. Employees must maintain work authorization without sponsorship for the duration of their appointment. Work safely at all times, which includes but is not limited to, participating and completing all required safety trainings, as well as performing all job tasks in accordance with Minnesota State University, Mankato policies and procedures utilizing appropriate tools, equipment and personal protective equipment. The Minnesota State University, Mankato Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available for your review. This report is required by federal law and contains policy statements and crime statistics for the University. The policy statements address the school’s policies, procedures and programs concerning safety and security. Three years’ worth of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that were reported to have occurred on-campus, or in other University affiliated locations. This report is available online at: http://www.mnsu.edu/safety/ . You may also request a paper copy from University Security at 507-389-2111, or by emailing security@mnsu.edu . Minimal travel required. Up to 5% of the time. Work Shift (Hours / Days of work) Monday - Friday, 8:00 - 4:30 PM Telework (Yes/No) Yes - Up to 95% of the time. Based on the essential functions of this positions, MMB Policy #1422, and University policies relating to flexible work, this position is eligible for the following work modes: Telework: A position with a work arrangement that allows an employee to perform work on a regular basis at a telework location that is not the employee’s permanent/principal work location. About More than 1600 talented faculty, staff, and 1600 student employees with a wide variety of skills and backgrounds, support university operations every day. Our faculty and staff enjoy excellent benefits, a team environment and challenging careers. As an affirmative action/equal opportunity institution, we are committed to supporting the continued growth of our diverse community. Destination 2030 , the University’s strategic plan announced by President Edward Inch in August 2023, commits the University to making transformative strides in four main areas: being a lifelong provider of access to an equitable and affordable education; being a leader in transformational learning generating inspired action; being a nimble and innovative steward of resources; and being a community of care built upon diversity, inclusion, and belonging. Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 12-02-2026 Position End Date: Open Date: 08-17-2026 Close Date: 09-29-2026 Posting Contact Name: Sarith Phan Posting Contact Email: sarith.phan@mnsu.edu"
    },
    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mankato/Program-Advisor---MSUAASF-Range-B--AA27072-_JR0000005397": {
      "title": "Program Advisor - MSUAASF Range B (AA27072)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Program Advisor - MSUAASF Range B (AA27072) Institution: Minnesota State University, Mankato Classification Title: MSUAASF Range B Bargaining Unit / Union: 211: Minnesota State University Association of Administrative Service Faculty City: Mankato FLSA: Non Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Part time Employment Condition: Unclassified - Limited Academic (Fixed Term) Salary Range: Salary Range: $48,027.00 - $78,850.00 Salary Type: Depends on Qualifications Application Deadline: Review of applications will begin on September 9, 2026, and continue until the position has been filled. Position: Probationary; Range B* Job Description This is an outreach position that works out of Minnesota State University, Mankato. Its purpose is to provide grant specified services to low-income, potential first-generation college students from southcentral Minnesota high schools. The Advisor will implement tutoring and advising sessions at target schools; maintain records; evaluate students; develop curriculum; recruit students for the program; interact with target school personnel; work on program publications; plan/coordinate monthly Saturday Sessions. This is a grant position and is contingent upon continued funding. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree in Education or a related field (Conferred on an official transcript at the time of application). Knowledge and understanding of federal rules and regulations One year of experience working with high school students Experience in developing curriculum and student activities Ability to administer, evaluate and interpret standardized tests and inventories Demonstrated ability to communicate well in writing and verbally Familiarity with the secondary education system and current trends Ability to teach and deliver services remotely Demonstrated ability to work with program participants from diverse backgrounds in groups and individually. Preferred Qualification  Demonstrated commitment to fostering a diverse working and learning environment. One year working with TRIO programs APPLICATION PROCEDURES: A complete online application must include all required attachments. Incomplete applications will not be reviewed by the search committee. Please note that, due to Workday system limitations, you may upload a maximum of five (5) attachments with your application. If you need to submit more than five attachments, please contact us directly and we will assist with uploading the additional documents on your behalf. Cover Letter Non-Photo Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for three (3) references Unofficial Transcript(s) of your highest completed degree A brief (no more than one-page) diversity statement presenting a commitment to or experience working in an equity-minded environment Other Requirements Please note that successful applicants must be eligible to work in the United States on or before the effective date of appointment. Eligibility includes being a U.S. citizen or national, a lawful permanent resident, or a foreign national authorized to work in the U.S. without the need for employer sponsorship. Employees must maintain work authorization without sponsorship for the duration of their appointment. Work safely at all times, which includes but is not limited to, participating and completing all required safety trainings, as well as performing all job tasks in accordance with Minnesota State University, Mankato policies and procedures utilizing appropriate tools, equipment and personal protective equipment. The Minnesota State University, Mankato Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available for your review. This report is required by federal law and contains policy statements and crime statistics for the University. The policy statements address the school’s policies, procedures and programs concerning safety and security. Three years’ worth of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that were reported to have occurred on-campus, or in other University affiliated locations. This report is available online at: http://www.mnsu.edu/safety/ . You may also request a paper copy from University Security at 507-389-2111, or by emailing security@mnsu.edu . This position requires a valid, applicable driver’s license, as well as a DVS records check with an acceptable rating. Employees must have an active, valid, and, applicable driver’s license if they drive a vehicle on state business. For further information, please refer to the Driver’s License and Record Check Policy (HR/LR Policy #1419), which can be found at: https://mn.gov/mmb-stat/policies/1419-hrpolicy-dlrchecks.pdf . This position requires a passing background check under Minnesota Statutes 299C.66 to 299C.71 – Kari Koskinen Manager Background Check Act. It is expected that the employee maintains the ability to pass applicable background check throughout employment. It is the employee’s responsibility to notify the supervisor no later than the beginning of your next shift of any charges, allegations, convictions that may impact their standing under the applicable background check. Travel to and from target schools with the use of state vehicle. May occasionally work irregular hours during Saturday Sessions and other program events. Lifting and carrying program equipment and materials up 45 pounds. Telework (Yes/No) Based on the essential functions of this positions, MMB Policy #1422, and University policies relating to flexible work, this position is eligible for the following work modes: Mobile Work: Up to 80% of the time. A position where the employee travels continuously for work, or who performs work at multiple locations outside of an agency office, such as a field location or other site. About Additional information on Minnesota State University, Mankato can be found at: www.mnsu.edu . The salary range denoted above is the contractual range; however, salary upon hire is dependent upon qualifications and experience. University Demographics Minnesota State University, Mankato is a member of the Minnesota State system. Minnesota State has established a strategic vision, Equity 2030, which aims to close the educational equity gaps across race and ethnicity, socioeconomic status, ability, and geographic location by the end of the decade at every Minnesota State college and university and to provide an opportunity for all Minnesotans to create a better future for themselves, for their families, and for their communities. The focus of the work includes: · Enhancing access and student success. · Providing Minnesota with the talent it needs. · Anchoring the communities and regions we serve. Equity 2030 seeks to bridge efforts occurring within divisions and institutions, creating an intentional statewide culture of equity-minded collaboration and resulting in equitable practice embedded throughout our institutions. The full Equity 2030 plan is linked here: https://www.minnstate.edu/Equity2030/index.html . Destination 2030 , the University’s strategic plan announced by President Edward Inch in August 2023, commits the University to making transformative strides in four main areas: being a lifelong provider of access to an equitable and affordable education; being a leader in transformational learning generating inspired action; being a nimble and innovative steward of resources; and being a community of care built upon diversity, inclusion, and belonging. We seek to attract teacher-scholars who will be culturally and academically diverse faculty members, and staff with a demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. Minnesota State University, Mankato, is student-centered and focuses on applied research that expands knowledge; improves learning; and serves the region, state, and nation. Founded as a Normal School in 1868, Minnesota State University, Mankato is now the second largest university in Minnesota with a tradition of combining big-ideas with real-world thinking to find solutions for pressing problems in the state, region, and global society. Mankato, Minnesota, is a community of nearly 44,500 people, about 85 miles southwest of the twin cities of Minneapolis and St. Paul. The University acknowledges the land and the tribal nations upon this land whose work is being accomplished. We acknowledge that we are on Dakota land. We also take the opportunity to recognize that we live, work, and learn in the homeland of the Dakota people, whose language frames our name—Minnesota State University, Mankato. Serving approximately 17,900 students annually, the University is an applied research institution, with more than 200 academic programs, from bachelor’s through doctoral degrees. The University is a diverse and global campus with 18% students of color and1,175 + international students from 95 countries, cutting-edge information technology solutions and extensive partnerships, with 1,600 faculty and staff, including 700 teaching faculty. The University has additional locations and a growing number of on-line programs to accelerate educational access and opportunity. These locations include partnerships in northern Minnesota’s the iron range region. Fast facts about the university can be found here: https://mankato.mnsu.edu/about-the-university/fast-facts/ . CONTACT INFORMATION: Chris Corley Library and Learning Phone: 507-389-5955 TTY: 800-627-3529 or 711 Email: christopher.corley@mnsu.edu *Employment for this position is covered by the collective bargaining agreement for the Minnesota State University Administrative and Service Faculty which can be found at: https://admin.mnsu.edu/human-resources/our-benefits/bargaining-units-and-personnel-plans/ NOTICE: In accordance with the Minnesota State Vehicle Fleet Safety Program, employees driving on college/university business who use a rental or state vehicle shall be required to conform to MN State’s vehicle use criteria and consent to a Motor Vehicle Records check. Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 12-02-2026 Position End Date: 08-31-2027 Open Date: 08-20-2026 Close Date: 09-09-2026 Posting Contact Name: Sarith Phan Posting Contact Email: sarith.phan@mnsu.edu"
    },
    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mankato/Assistant-Director--Accessibility-Resources---MSUAASF-Range-C--DI27002-_JR0000005525": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Accessibility Resources - MSUAASF Range C (DI27002)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Assistant Director, Accessibility Resources - MSUAASF Range C (DI27002) Institution: Minnesota State University, Mankato Classification Title: MSUAASF Range C Bargaining Unit / Union: 211: Minnesota State University Association of Administrative Service Faculty City: Mankato FLSA: Non Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Unclassified - Unlimited Academic Salary Range: $47,845.00 - $93,809.00 Application Deadline: Review of applications will begin on August 31, 2026 and continue until the position has been filled. POSITION: Probationary; Range C* Job Description The Assistant Director in Accessibility Resources is responsible for ensuring the University's compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and Sec. 504, of the Rehabilitation Act. The Assistant Director will share the responsibility of the design and assessment of projects and the formulation and implementation of office goals and objectives. They will share in the supervision of student employees that aid in students with learning disabilities, ADHD, mental health conditions, pregnancy, parenting challenges, and visual impairment. They will be responsible for working with Residential Life on student housing accommodations and the University Title IX coordinator on student accommodations, as well as support student experiencing medical emergencies. The Assistant Director works with enrollment management of Accessibility Resource specific student population, and campus-wide Student Success partners across the University. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Education, Social Work, Psychology or related field plus two (2) years of professional experience working with students with disabilities in a secondary or post-secondary educational system or equivalent combination of post-secondary training, education, and/or professional experience. Knowledge of psycho-educational test instruments at the level necessary to review and interpret diagnostic results to determine the presence of a disability per university criteria and to determine appropriate accommodations. Knowledge of Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) of 1990, the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA) and other appropriate laws on higher education and disability. Preferred Qualification  Demonstrated commitment to fostering a diverse working and learning environment. Master's degree in Special Education, College Student Personnel, Psychology, Rehabilitation Counseling or related field, and at least two (2) years of related experience. Demonstrated commitment to fostering a diverse working and learning environment. Strong presentation, oral, and written communication skills. Ability to direct and organize work of self and others. Ability to collaborate with others. Strong computer skills, including all MS applications and database management software. APPLICATION PROCEDURES: A complete online application will include the following attachments. Incomplete applications will not be reviewed by the search committee. Cover Letter Non-Photo Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for three (3) references Unofficial Transcript(s) of your highest completed degree A brief (no more than one-page) diversity statement presenting a commitment to or experience working in an equity-minded environment Other Requirements The University may be able to provide employment visa sponsorship for qualified candidates, subject to USCIS guidelines and eligibility requirements. Work safely at all times, which includes but is not limited to, participating and completing all required safety trainings, as well as performing all job tasks in accordance with Minnesota State University, Mankato policies and procedures utilizing appropriate tools, equipment and personal protective equipment. The Minnesota State University, Mankato Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available for your review. This report is required by federal law and contains policy statements and crime statistics for the University. The policy statements address the school’s policies, procedures and programs concerning safety and security. Three years’ worth of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that were reported to have occurred on-campus, or in other University affiliated locations. This report is available online at: http://www.mnsu.edu/safety/ . You may also request a paper copy from University Security at 507-389-2111, or by emailing security@mnsu.edu . This position requires a valid, applicable driver’s license, as well as DVS records check with an acceptable rating. Telework Yes - Up to 20% of the time. Based on the essential functions of this position, MMB Policy #1422, and University policies relating to flexible work, this position is eligible for the following work modes: Telework: A position with a work arrangement that allows an employee to perform work on a regular basis at a telework location that is not the employee’s permanent/principal work location. About Additional information on Minnesota State University, Mankato can be found at: www.mnsu.edu . The salary range denoted above is the contractual range; however, salary upon hire is dependent upon qualifications and experience. University Demographics Minnesota State University, Mankato is a member of the Minnesota State system. Minnesota State has established a strategic vision, Equity 2030, which aims to close the educational equity gaps across race and ethnicity, socioeconomic status, ability, and geographic location by the end of the decade at every Minnesota State college and university and to provide an opportunity for all Minnesotans to create a better future for themselves, for their families, and for their communities. The focus of the work includes: · Enhancing access and student success. · Providing Minnesota with the talent it needs. · Anchoring the communities and regions we serve. Equity 2030 seeks to bridge efforts occurring within divisions and institutions, creating an intentional statewide culture of equity-minded collaboration and resulting in equitable practice embedded throughout our institutions. The full Equity 2030 plan is linked here: https://www.minnstate.edu/Equity2030/index.html . Destination 2030 , the University’s strategic plan announced by President Edward Inch in August 2023, commits the University to making transformative strides in four main areas: being a lifelong provider of access to an equitable and affordable education; being a leader in transformational learning generating inspired action; being a nimble and innovative steward of resources; and being a community of care built upon diversity, inclusion, and belonging. We seek to attract teacher-scholars who will be culturally and academically diverse faculty members, and staff with a demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. Minnesota State University, Mankato, is student-centered and focuses on applied research that expands knowledge; improves learning; and serves the region, state, and nation. Founded as a Normal School in 1868, Minnesota State University, Mankato is now the second largest university in Minnesota with a tradition of combining big-ideas with real-world thinking to find solutions for pressing problems in the state, region, and global society. Mankato, Minnesota, is a community of nearly 44,500 people, about 85 miles southwest of the twin cities of Minneapolis and St. Paul. The University acknowledges the land and the tribal nations upon this land whose work is being accomplished. We acknowledge that we are on Dakota land. We also take the opportunity to recognize that we live, work, and learn in the homeland of the Dakota people, whose language frames our name—Minnesota State University, Mankato. Serving approximately 17,900 students annually, the University is an applied research institution, with more than 200 academic programs, from bachelor’s through doctoral degrees. The University is a diverse and global campus with 18% students of color and1,175 + international students from 95 countries, cutting-edge information technology solutions and extensive partnerships, with 1,600 faculty and staff, including 700 teaching faculty. The University has additional locations and a growing number of on-line programs to accelerate educational access and opportunity. These locations include partnerships in northern Minnesota’s the iron range region. Fast facts about the university can be found here: https://mankato.mnsu.edu/about-the-university/fast-facts/ . CONTACT INFORMATION: Carine Omole, Senior Director of Accessibility Resources and ADA Compliance Officer Minnesota State University, Mankato Mankato, MN 56001 Phone: 507-389-1819 TTY: 800-627-3529 or 711 Email: carine.omole@mnsu.edu . *Employment for this position is covered by the collective bargaining agreement for the Minnesota State University Administrative and Service Faculty which can be found at: https://admin.mnsu.edu/human-resources/our-benefits/bargaining-units-and-personnel-plans/ NOTICE: In accordance with the Minnesota State Vehicle Fleet Safety Program, employees driving on college/university business who use a rental or state vehicle shall be required to conform to MN State’s vehicle use criteria and consent to a Motor Vehicle Records check. Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 10-12-2026 Position End Date: Open Date: 08-10-2026 Close Date: 12-31-2026 Posting Contact Name: Lacie R Mitchell-Garza Posting Contact Email: lacie.mitchell-garza@mnsu.edu"
    },
    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mankato/Program-and-Student-Support-Coordinator---MSUAASF-Range-C--AA26154-_JR0000004623-1": {
      "title": "Program and Student Support Coordinator - MSUAASF Range C (AA26154)  & (AA26157)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Program and Student Support Coordinator - MSUAASF Range C (AA26154) & (AA26157) Institution: Minnesota State University, Mankato Classification Title: MSUAASF Range C Bargaining Unit / Union: 211: Minnesota State University Association of Administrative Service Faculty City: Mankato FLSA: Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Unclassified - Unlimited Academic Salary Range: $47,845.00 - $93,809.00 *2 OPEN Positions: PRF#s: AA26154 & AA26157 Application Deadline: Review of applications will begin on May 14, 2026 and continue until the position has been filled. POSITION: Probationary; Range C* Job Description Provide professional support to all students in the program while collaborating with faculty to foster positive advising experiences that will provide personal growth, practical skills, knowledge, and experience in preparation for future employment within various Aviation career fields.  Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in an Aviation discipline or closely related field and a minimum of one (1) year experience in an aviation environment, which may include military, industry (airline, corporate, or airport), educational or professional aviation training (teaching at flight school or academy) or in higher education OR a minimum of an AAS degree and a minimum of three (3) years' experience in an aviation environment or in a higher education environment. Valid driver's license required Preferred Qualification  Demonstrated commitment to fostering a diverse working and learning environment. Strong background or experience in the field of aviation. Background or experience in advising, career development or similar field Experience teaching in a formal setting (higher education, corporate training and development, etc) Excellent communication, interpersonal and presentation skills. Experience with basic student learning assessment practices. Demonstrated ability to supervise students, or strong potential for successful supervision. Knowledge of accreditation practices or potential to learn accreditation practices. APPLICATION PROCEDURES: A complete online application will include the following attachments. Incomplete applications will not be reviewed by the search committee. Cover Letter Non-Photo Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for three (3) references Unofficial Transcript(s) of your highest completed degree A brief (no more than one-page) diversity statement presenting a commitment to or experience working in an equity-minded environment Other Requirements Work safely at all times, which includes but is not limited to, participating and completing all required safety trainings, as well as performing all job tasks in accordance with Minnesota State University, Mankato policies and procedures utilizing appropriate tools, equipment and personal protective equipment. The Minnesota State University, Mankato Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available for your review. This report is required by federal law and contains policy statements and crime statistics for the University. The policy statements address the school’s policies, procedures and programs concerning safety and security. Three years’ worth of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that were reported to have occurred on-campus, or in other University affiliated locations. This report is available online at: http://www.mnsu.edu/safety/ . You may also request a paper copy from University Security at 507-389-2111, or by emailing security@mnsu.edu . Assignments may include evening or weekend advising/orientation duties by the individual, or supervision of a Graduate Assistant (GA) that assists with accreditation site visits. It is possible certain advising or accreditation site visit prep may need to be done the evening prior to the date of the visit This position requires a valid, applicable driver’s license, as well as DVS records check with an acceptable rating. Telework No - Based on the essential functions of this position, MMB Policy #1422, and University policies relating to flexible work, this position is eligible for the following work modes: Exclusively on Campus. A position that requires the employee to perform all their work at their campus work location. About Additional information on Minnesota State University, Mankato can be found at: www.mnsu.edu . The salary range denoted above is the contractual range; however, salary upon hire is dependent upon qualifications and experience. University Demographics Minnesota State University, Mankato is a member of the Minnesota State system. Minnesota State has established a strategic vision, Equity 2030, which aims to close the educational equity gaps across race and ethnicity, socioeconomic status, ability, and geographic location by the end of the decade at every Minnesota State college and university and to provide an opportunity for all Minnesotans to create a better future for themselves, for their families, and for their communities. The focus of the work includes: · Enhancing access and student success. · Providing Minnesota with the talent it needs. · Anchoring the communities and regions we serve. Equity 2030 seeks to bridge efforts occurring within divisions and institutions, creating an intentional statewide culture of equity-minded collaboration and resulting in equitable practice embedded throughout our institutions. The full Equity 2030 plan is linked here: https://www.minnstate.edu/Equity2030/index.html . Destination 2030 , the University’s strategic plan announced by President Edward Inch in August 2023, commits the University to making transformative strides in four main areas: being a lifelong provider of access to an equitable and affordable education; being a leader in transformational learning generating inspired action; being a nimble and innovative steward of resources; and being a community of care built upon diversity, inclusion, and belonging. We seek to attract teacher-scholars who will be culturally and academically diverse faculty members, and staff with a demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. Minnesota State University, Mankato, is student-centered and focuses on applied research that expands knowledge; improves learning; and serves the region, state, and nation. Founded as a Normal School in 1868, Minnesota State University, Mankato is now the second largest university in Minnesota with a tradition of combining big-ideas with real-world thinking to find solutions for pressing problems in the state, region, and global society. Mankato, Minnesota, is a community of nearly 44,500 people, about 85 miles southwest of the twin cities of Minneapolis and St. Paul. The University acknowledges the land and the tribal nations upon this land whose work is being accomplished. We acknowledge that we are on Dakota land. We also take the opportunity to recognize that we live, work, and learn in the homeland of the Dakota people, whose language frames our name—Minnesota State University, Mankato. Serving approximately 17,900 students annually, the University is an applied research institution, with more than 200 academic programs, from bachelor’s through doctoral degrees. The University is a diverse and global campus with 18% students of color and1,175 + international students from 95 countries, cutting-edge information technology solutions and extensive partnerships, with 1,600 faculty and staff, including 700 teaching faculty. The University has additional locations and a growing number of on-line programs to accelerate educational access and opportunity. These locations include partnerships in northern Minnesota’s the iron range region. Fast facts about the university can be found here: https://mankato.mnsu.edu/about-the-university/fast-facts/ . CONTACT INFORMATION: Jake Veness, Director of Operations & Logistics Aviation Department Minnesota State University, Mankato Mankato, MN 56001 Phone: 507-389-1056 TTY: 800-627-3529 or 711 Email: jacob.veness.2@mnsu.edu *Employment for this position is covered by the collective bargaining agreement for the Minnesota State University Administrative and Service Faculty which can be found at: https://admin.mnsu.edu/human-resources/our-benefits/bargaining-units-and-personnel-plans/ NOTICE: In accordance with the Minnesota State Vehicle Fleet Safety Program, employees driving on college/university business who use a rental or state vehicle shall be required to conform to MN State’s vehicle use criteria and consent to a Motor Vehicle Records check. Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 06-23-2026 Position End Date: Open Date: 04-23-2026 Close Date: 09-30-2026 Posting Contact Name: Lacie R Mitchell-Garza Posting Contact Email: lacie.mitchell-garza@mnsu.edu"
