    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mankato/Partnerships-and-Student-Support-Coordinator---MSUAASF-Range-C--AA26155-_JR0000004865": {
      "title": "Partnerships and Student Support Coordinator - MSUAASF Range C (AA26155)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Partnerships and Student Support Coordinator - MSUAASF Range C (AA26155) Institution: Minnesota State University, Mankato Classification Title: MSUAASF Range C Bargaining Unit / Union: 211: Minnesota State University Association of Administrative Service Faculty City: Mankato FLSA: Non Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Unclassified - Unlimited Academic Salary Range: $47,607.00 - $93,342.00 Application Deadline: Review of applications will begin on June 4, 2026 and continue until the position has been filled. POSITION: Probationary; Range C* Job Description The Partnerships and Student Support Coordinator will facilitate the development and maintenance of collaborative relationships with P-12 partners, higher education and other stakeholders to advance the college’s vision, commitment and values. Working closely with the Dean of the College of Education, this position provides support for the ongoing growth of the Minnesota Educator Partnerships (MEP) and will also seek opportunities to develop partnerships in support of the Counseling and Student Personnel and Aviation departments as well as special initiatives defined by the dean.  This position also collaborates with the Office of Field and International Experience to assist in the placement, supervision, and evaluation of student teachers and field experience candidates.     Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in education plus a minimum of three (3) years of professional experience in teaching, education, leadership, or outreach.  Experience in strategic program planning and implementation, leading change management and process improvement methods.  Ability to work collaboratively across divisions and colleges with personnel at all levels.  Demonstrated ability to work with students of 